refactor: remove dead code found by a full-repo audit

Four parallel reviewers swept the Rust backend and the TS frontend,
cross-checking every definition against real call sites rather than
trusting reference counts. Everything removed below had zero production
callers; anything merely test-only was reported but left in place.

Rust:
- we_client: is_installed, get_config_key, save_properties,
  delete_wallpaper_folder (+ its test) — superseded by the command-layer
  implementations that are actually wired up.
- accounts: list_usernames, username_at — list_detailed and credentials
  cover every caller.
- webview: unused jar() accessor.

Commands registered in lib.rs but never invoked from the frontend:
  steam_login_hide, steam_login_reveal, steam_login_fill,
  steam_save_session, app_get_data_dir, app_minimize,
  app_get_window_geometry, config_save_window_geometry,
  accounts_get_current, accounts_set_current, accounts_reset_custom,
  metadata_save, metadata_remove, we_detect, we_current_pubfileid,
  we_set_volume, download_status_all, extract_status_all, dotnet_get_root.
Their Tauri registration and implementations are gone; the functionality
they duplicated lives elsewhere (events, or the command that is used).

Frontend:
- lib/videoStream.ts: getStreamPlayer, stopVideoStream,
  stopAllVideoStreams and the now-unused PlayerInfo type.

Also kept the historical note in webview.rs explaining why the hidden
window uses decorations(false)/shadow(false): it documents a real DWM
artefact that used to flash translucent rectangles over the app, and
removing the reasoning would invite someone to undo the fix.

Gates: cargo fmt/clippy/test 52 passed, tsc 0, eslint 0, vitest 113.